{:id :EACL-FORMAL-073
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "unsupported-spicedb-subject-relation/silently-authorized-as-base-object"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :false-grant
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before unsupported subject-relation validation"]
 :affected-backends
 [:shared :datomic :datahike :datalevin :datascript :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "Public endpoint validation admitted a non-nil :relation field even though EACL does not implement SpiceDB subject#relation usersets. Identity resolution then used only :type and :id, silently changing the caller's object into the base object and potentially authorizing that different identity."
 :fix
 "Reject every non-nil endpoint :relation before dispatch across scalar and batch checks, lookup and scan filters, permission-tree expansion, relationship mutation, and object deletion; bind the rule with a Dafny request-boundary model, an executed mutation, and a real DataScript regression."
 :closing-evidence
 ["PublicRequestBoundary.OpenEndpointAcceptedUnsupportedSubjectRelation"
  "PublicRequestBoundary.StrictEndpointRejectsUnsupportedSubjectRelation"
  "eacl.formal.executed-mutation-controls/unsupported-subject-relation-downgrade-killed?"
  "eacl.datascript.contract-test/unsupported-subject-relations-never-degrade-to-base-objects-test"]}
